  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1106 AM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\n16z surface analysis had trough from eastern MT to central CO. \nWater vapour loop had upper ridge from NM into eastern MT/WY with \na couple of ridge-riders over southeast MT and western WY/UT. \n0.5km 1-minute visible satellite loop showed most activity was \nelevated at this point, although there is a CU field over south- \ncentral SD associated with oppressive Td/s in the lower 70s. \nEffects of these features the main short term forecast concern.\n\nThis afternoon/tonight, heat indices will be in the lower 100s \neast of the Black Hills so hoisted a Heat Advisory earlier to \naccount. Main shortwave rotates around upper ridge later this \nafternoon and evening. At least 1-2KJ/kg MLCAPE pools ahead of \nsurface trough with 25-35kts of effective shear forecast. Bufkit \nsoundings suggest damaging winds would be the main threat with \nsevere convection (marginal to slight (1-2 out of 5)) risk over \nCWA, highest over northwestern SD. Latest CAMs/HREF emphasize this\nthinking. So, expect a couple clusters of severe convection this \nafternoon/evening moving across the CWA. If cold pools can \ncongeal, could see a line of severe thunderstorms for a period \nwhich some CAM solutions suggest. Activity will weaken overnight, \nbut decent low level jet likely to sustain convection. \nTemperatures will be near guidance.\n\nThursday, compact mid-level circulation moves across the CWA with\ncontinued chances for thunderstorms as a cold front slices \nthrough the area leading to \"cooler\" temperatures. Cold front may \nbe focus for active/severe thunderstorms Thursday afternoon over \nsouth-central SD. Temperatures will be near guidance.\n\nLingering PoPs Friday given way to robust thermal ridge expansion\nfor the weekend with Sunday highs from 100-110F putting pressure \non some records. Mostly dry, but it is the northern Plains, so \nthunderstorms cannot be completely ruled out. Next week looks \n\"cooler\" as upper ridge flattens and west/northwest flow aloft \ndevelops, sure to provide shortwaves to create daily chances of \nthunderstorms. Confidence is growing for the brief cooldown.",
